IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `esos-student`

-- The Minister's ESOS instruments -- the refund amounts (ss 46D(7), 47E(4)), the suitable alternative course criteria
-- (s 49(6)) and the national code's requirements for the written agreement (ss 33, 47B), read from the deposited instruments.
-- A module beside esos-student.l4; it computes the refund amount that module gives a due day and payee for, and decides the
-- "agreement that meets s 47B" fact it asks, restating none of its rules.
--
-- SEAT: the overseas student, as in esos-student.l4. "I paid $18,000 of tuition fees. My provider failed to start the course,
-- or I withdrew with no compliant written agreement, or my visa was refused: how much must the provider refund me?"
--
-- Editions, all deposited 2026-10-23 as their own subjects with parent_act this Act:
--  * Education Services for Overseas Students (Calculation of Refund) Instrument 2024, as made (F2024L01231), at
--    ../../../education-services-for-overseas-students-calculation-of-refund-instrument-2024/registers/source-bundle/
--    F2024L01231.txt, with its formulas (images in the authorised rendering) in F2024L01231.formulas.md beside it;
--  * Education Services for Overseas Students (Suitable Alternative Courses) Instrument 2022, as made (F2022L01299);
--  * National Code of Practice for Providers of Education and Training to Overseas Students 2018, latest compilation No. 1
--    (F2026C00148, 21 January 2026; the Register had no document for "Current" on 23 October 2026, so a later amendment,
--    F2026L01351, may be missing: see its SOURCE-LICENSE.md). Standard 3 only.
--
-- UNITS. The Calculation of Refund Instrument counts calendar days and gives its own roundings (ss 6(2), 7(2)). The student
-- states the two day counts the formulas name, in the instrument's own words; the module does not choose whether a count
-- includes its first or last day (NOTES.md finding 19).

§ `ESOS instruments -- how much is my refund`

§§ `Calculation of Refund Instrument 2024, ss 6, 7 -- the weekly fee and the weeks`

-- "If the fee calculated under subsection (1) is not a whole dollar amount, round the fee up to the nearest whole dollar"
-- (s 6(2)); "If the number of weeks ... is not a whole number, round the number up to the nearest whole number" (s 7(2)).
GIVEN x IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`rounded up to a whole number` MEANS
    IF TRUNC x 0 EQUALS x THEN x ELSE TRUNC x 0 PLUS 1

-- s 6(1), formula (F2024L01231.formulas.md, image2): weekly tuition fee = total tuition fees for the course / number of
-- calendar days in the course x 7.
GIVEN `total tuition fees for the course` IS A NUMBER
      `number of calendar days in the course` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the weekly tuition fee` MEANS
    `rounded up to a whole number` ((`total tuition fees for the course` DIVIDED BY `number of calendar days in the course`) TIMES 7)

-- s 7(1), formula (image3): weeks in default period = number of calendar days from the default day to the end of the period
-- to which the payment relates / 7; only weeks "for which the provider received payment of tuition fees".
GIVEN `calendar days from the default day to the end of the paid period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the weeks in default period` MEANS
    `rounded up to a whole number` (`calendar days from the default day to the end of the paid period` DIVIDED BY 7)

-- ss 8, 9, 10(4), formula (image4): refund amount = weekly tuition fee x weeks in default period.
GIVEN `total tuition fees for the course` IS A NUMBER
      `number of calendar days in the course` IS A NUMBER
      `calendar days from the default day to the end of the paid period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the instrument refund` MEANS
    `the weekly tuition fee` `total tuition fees for the course` `number of calendar days in the course`
    TIMES `the weeks in default period` `calendar days from the default day to the end of the paid period`

@export What is my "weekly tuition fee" under the Calculation of Refund Instrument (s 6)?
GIVEN `total tuition fees for the course` IS A NUMBER @desc The total tuition fees for the whole course, in dollars
      `number of calendar days in the course` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of calendar days in the course
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my weekly tuition fee` MEANS `the weekly tuition fee` `total tuition fees for the course` `number of calendar days in the course`

§§ `s 46D(6), (7); Instrument s 8 -- my provider defaulted`

-- s 8: "For the purposes of subsection 46D(6) of the Act, the amount of a refund of tuition fees received by a registered
-- provider in respect of a student is calculated as follows" (image4). The refund cannot exceed what the provider received:
-- s 7(1)(b) counts only weeks "for which the provider received payment of tuition fees".
@export My provider defaulted. How much of my unspent tuition fees must it refund (s 46D(6), Instrument s 8)?
GIVEN `total tuition fees for the course` IS A NUMBER @desc The total tuition fees for the whole course, in dollars
      `number of calendar days in the course` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of calendar days in the course
      `calendar days from the default day to the end of the paid period` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of calendar days from the default day to the end of the period your tuition payment covered (the period the provider was paid for)
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much must my defaulting provider refund` MEANS
    `the instrument refund` `total tuition fees for the course` `number of calendar days in the course` `calendar days from the default day to the end of the paid period`

§§ `s 47E; Instrument ss 9, 10 -- I defaulted, with no compliant agreement or after a visa refusal`

DECLARE `Why the refund is under s 47E` IS ONE OF
    `the provider never entered into a written agreement with me that meets s 47B`
    `my student visa was refused, so I did not start the course on the agreed day`
    `my student visa was refused, so I withdrew or did not pay`

-- s 9 (no compliant agreement): image4. s 10(2) (visa refused, not started): "the amount of the course fees, minus the lesser of
-- the following amounts: (a) 5% of the amount of course fees received by the provider in respect of the student before the
-- default day; (b) $500"; (3): course fees = tuition fees plus non-tuition fees received. s 10(4) (visa refused, withdrew or
-- did not pay): image4.
GIVEN `why` IS A `Why the refund is under s 47E`
      `total tuition fees for the course` IS A NUMBER
      `number of calendar days in the course` IS A NUMBER
      `calendar days from the default day to the end of the paid period` IS A NUMBER
      `tuition fees received` IS A NUMBER
      `non-tuition fees received` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 47E refund` MEANS
    IF `why` EQUALS `my student visa was refused, so I did not start the course on the agreed day`
    THEN `the course fees` MINUS `the lesser deduction`
    ELSE `the instrument refund` `total tuition fees for the course` `number of calendar days in the course` `calendar days from the default day to the end of the paid period`
    WHERE
        `the course fees` MEANS `tuition fees received` PLUS `non-tuition fees received`
        `five per cent` MEANS `the course fees` TIMES 0.05
        `the lesser deduction` MEANS IF `five per cent` LESS THAN 500 THEN `five per cent` ELSE 500

@export I defaulted on my course and the refund is under s 47E. How much must my provider refund me (s 47E(2), Instrument ss 9, 10)?
GIVEN `why` IS A `Why the refund is under s 47E` @desc Why s 47E applies: no written agreement meeting s 47B; or a student visa refusal that stopped you starting; or one that made you withdraw or stop paying
      `total tuition fees for the course` IS A NUMBER @desc The total tuition fees for the whole course, in dollars
      `number of calendar days in the course` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of calendar days in the course
      `calendar days from the default day to the end of the paid period` IS A NUMBER @desc The number of calendar days from your default day to the end of the period your tuition payment covered
      `tuition fees received` IS A NUMBER @desc The tuition fees the provider received from you or for you before the default day
      `non-tuition fees received` IS A NUMBER @desc The non-tuition fees (for example enrolment or materials fees) the provider received before the default day; 0 if none
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much must my provider refund under s 47E` MEANS
    `the s 47E refund` `why` `total tuition fees for the course` `number of calendar days in the course` `calendar days from the default day to the end of the paid period` `tuition fees received` `non-tuition fees received`

§§ `National Code Standard 3, ss 33, 47B -- does my written agreement meet the requirements`

-- Standard 3: the agreement must be entered into "concurrently with or prior to accepting payment of tuition fees or
-- non-tuition fees", "signed or otherwise accepted by the student" (by a parent or guardian if under 18), and in plain English
-- must outline the course, start date, locations, modes, prerequisites, conditions, all tuition fees and periods and payment
-- options, non-tuition fees, privacy disclosures, complaints and appeals, the student's duty to keep a copy, and must include
-- the refund information: "amounts that may or may not be repaid", "processes for claiming a refund", the specified persons
-- who may receive one, "a plain English explanation of what happens in the event of a course not being delivered, including
-- the role of the TPS", and the Australian Consumer Law statement; and a requirement that the student notify contact details
-- and changes "within 7 days of the change".
@export Does my written agreement with my provider meet the national code, so that it can set my refund (s 47B, National Code Standard 3)?
GIVEN `it was made before or when I first paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you signed or accepted the written agreement no later than when the provider first accepted payment of fees from you
      `it was accepted by me, or my parent or guardian if I was under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you accepted it (or, if you were under 18, your parent or legal guardian did)
      `it sets out the course, fees and other matters the code lists` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether in plain English it outlines the course, start date, locations and modes, prerequisites, conditions, all tuition and non-tuition fees and payment options, privacy disclosures, complaints and appeals, and that you must keep a copy
      `it sets out the refund information the code lists` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it states the amounts that may or may not be repaid, how to claim a refund, any other person who may receive a refund, what happens if the course is not delivered (including the Tuition Protection Service's role), and the Australian Consumer Law statement
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Does my agreement meet the national code` IF
        `it was made before or when I first paid`
    AND `it was accepted by me, or my parent or guardian if I was under 18`
    AND `it sets out the course, fees and other matters the code lists`
    AND `it sets out the refund information the code lists`

@export I have defaulted on my course. What refund must my provider pay, to whom and by when, once the national code is applied to my agreement (ss 47B, 47D, 47E)?
GIVEN `the default day` IS A DATE @desc Your default day (the agreed starting day if you did not start; otherwise the day you withdrew or were refused)
      `it was made before or when I first paid` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you signed or accepted the written agreement no later than when the provider first accepted payment (FALSE if there is no agreement)
      `it was accepted by me, or my parent or guardian if I was under 18` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you (or your parent or guardian, if you were under 18) accepted it
      `it sets out the course, fees and other matters the code lists` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it outlines the course, fees and the other matters the code lists
      `it sets out the refund information the code lists` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it states the refund amounts, how to claim, who else may receive a refund, what happens if the course is not delivered, and the Australian Consumer Law statement
      `I was refused a student visa, which caused it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you were refused a student visa and that refusal was a reason you did not start, withdrew, or did not pay
      `the day of my written claim` IS A DATE @desc The day the provider received your written claim for the refund (only matters under a written agreement)
GIVETH A `My refund after my default`
`What refund after my default under the national code` MEANS
    `What refund must my provider pay after my default` `the default day` (`Does my agreement meet the national code` `it was made before or when I first paid` `it was accepted by me, or my parent or guardian if I was under 18` `it sets out the course, fees and other matters the code lists` `it sets out the refund information the code lists`) `I was refused a student visa, which caused it` `the day of my written claim`

§§ `Suitable Alternative Courses Instrument 2022 -- what the TPS Director weighs` -- arises only if the provider defaulted

-- s 6: "the criteria to be applied in considering whether a particular course is a 'suitable alternative course' are: (a)
-- whether the course is offered by a person who: (i) is registered under the Act to provide that particular course at the
-- location ...; or (ii) provides that course in accordance with an arrangement ... with a registered provider ...; (b) whether
-- the course is of a similar level of education and field of education as the course to which the default relates; (c)
-- geographical location; and (d) acceptability to the student." They are criteria the TPS Director applies, not conditions
-- that decide the question; the answer is given as whether each points towards the course.
DECLARE `The alternative course` IS ONE OF
    `every criterion points to it being suitable: registered (or arranged) provider, similar level and field, a workable location, and acceptable to me`
    `not every criterion points to it; the TPS Director weighs them (Suitable Alternative Courses Instrument s 6)`

@export The Tuition Protection Service offered me another course. Do the criteria for a "suitable alternative course" point to it (s 49(6), Instrument s 6)?
GIVEN `its provider is registered for it at that location, or arranged with one that is` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the course is offered by a provider registered to provide that course at that location, or under an arrangement with such a provider
      `it is of a similar level and field of education` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether it is of a similar level and field of education (Australian Standard Classification of Education) to your original course
      `its location suits me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether its geographical location is workable for you
      `it is acceptable to me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the course is acceptable to you
GIVETH A `The alternative course`
`Do the criteria point to a suitable alternative course` MEANS
    IF `its provider is registered for it at that location, or arranged with one that is` AND `it is of a similar level and field of education` AND `its location suits me` AND `it is acceptable to me`
    THEN `every criterion points to it being suitable: registered (or arranged) provider, similar level and field, a workable location, and acceptable to me`
    ELSE `not every criterion points to it; the TPS Director weighs them (Suitable Alternative Courses Instrument s 6)`

§§ `The duties, as rules`

DECLARE `ESOS party` IS ONE OF
    `my provider`
    `I, the student`

DECLARE `ESOS act` IS ONE OF
    `enter into a written agreement with me`
    `tell my provider my new contact details`
    `pay my refund`

-- Standard 3: "The registered provider must enter into a written agreement ... concurrently with or prior to accepting payment
-- of tuition fees or non-tuition fees." Counted from the moment the provider accepts a payment: the agreement must already
-- exist or be made at that moment, so the rule runs WITHIN 0 from then.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `ESOS party` `ESOS act`
`the agreement-before-payment duty` MEANS
    PARTY `my provider`
    MUST  `enter into a written agreement with me`
    WITHIN 0
    LEST  BREACH BY `my provider` BECAUSE "National Code Standard 3: no written agreement by the time fees were accepted"

-- Standard 3 requires the agreement to oblige the student to notify the provider of contact detail changes "within 7 days of
-- the change"; the duty is the student's, under the agreement.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `ESOS party` `ESOS act`
`my contact details duty` MEANS
    PARTY `I, the student`
    MUST  `tell my provider my new contact details`
    WITHIN 7
    LEST  BREACH BY `I, the student` BECAUSE "the written agreement (National Code Standard 3): changes of contact details must be notified within 7 days"

-- s 47E(3): the s 47E refund "within the period ... of 4 weeks after the default day", in the amount the Instrument sets.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `ESOS party` `ESOS act`
`the s 47E refund duty` MEANS
    PARTY `my provider`
    MUST  `pay my refund`
    WITHIN 28
    LEST  BREACH BY `my provider` BECAUSE "s 47E(3): the refund was not paid within 4 weeks after the default day; a call on the Overseas Students Tuition Fund follows (s 50A(4))"
